    "question": {
      ":question/id": "326f22b5-62b2-5527-a6a8-920954ee84a9",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1\\text{st},$ $3\\text{rd},$ and $4\\text{th}$ rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -1 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1\\text{st},$ $3\\text{rd},$ and $4\\text{th}$ rows of $A$ are $-5,$ $8,$ and $1$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -1 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-5+8+1=4.$",
